    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY. It does not say CReal.inv exists. It did not when this fact was written -- this fact is precisely about the shape its signature must have -- and it does now (ADR-0516, F:real-inverse-is-built-and-well-defined), with exactly the signature stated here. It does not say the reals apart from zero are exactly the reals not equal to zero: CReal.not_equiv_of_apart is ONE-WAY, and the converse is Markov's principle, which is neither proved nor assumed here. It does not say a Prop hypothesis blocks a Type-valued definition -- that reading is wrong, and the distinction is the point: a function may take a Prop and return a Type, it may not BRANCH on one, which is why the one-sided PosBound works where the disjunctive Apart does not.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "command": "python3 render/producers-py/facts_to_docir.py",
        "epoch": {
          "commit": "733126c0f351f0931f7eaf0b4f5f9f569f3aef44",
